schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Tokenomics
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The economics of a cryptocurrency or token system — how many tokens
    exist, how they are distributed, and what incentives are built in.
  source_traditions:
    - mechanism design / game theory
    - traditional monetary economics (supply, inflation)
    - token engineering (post-2018 DeFi practice)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Defined in the glossary's "T" section alongside Token, Transaction Fee,
    and Treasury; underlies design choices covered elsewhere in the toolkit
    (e.g. local-currency design questions of unit, backing, and issuance).
  adjacent_meanings:
    - token design (the mechanics of a single token's rules)
    - monetary policy (the macro discipline tokenomics borrows from)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Tokenomics ≠ Token — a token is the asset; tokenomics is the designed
      system of incentives, supply, and distribution around it
  tensions:
    - >-
      the glossary treats tokenomics as a neutral, technical discipline;
      elsewhere in web3 discourse "tokenomics" is often used to paper over
      extractive incentive design (Frame 1 language flagged in docs/CSIS.md)
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Reducing tokenomics to "supply, distribution, incentives" omits the
    value judgments embedded in any incentive design — who benefits from a
    given distribution schedule is a governance question, not just an
    economics one.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/key-terms-a-z.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
